---
import PrivacyLayout from "../../components/PrivacyLayout.astro";
---

<PrivacyLayout
    title="Privacy Policy - NStates App"
    appName="NStates"
    lastUpdated="10 February 2026"
    accentColor="#3498db"
>
    <div class="my-5 rounded-md border-l-4 border-emerald-500/80 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <strong>In summary:</strong> NStates is an Android client for the NationStates
        online nation simulation game. The app communicates exclusively with the official
        NationStates API. We do not collect, track, or share any personal data. There
        are no ads, analytics, or third-party tracking services.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        NStates is an unofficial Android client for
        <a href="https://www.nationstates.net" target="_blank" class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80">NationStates</a>,
        a free online nation simulation game. The app allows you to manage your
        nation, read and respond to issues, and view nation statistics from your
        Android device. NStates is not affiliated with or endorsed by NationStates
        or Max Barry.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data we do NOT collect</h2>
    <p>NStates does not directly collect, transmit, share, or sell:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Personally identifiable information</li>
        <li>App usage or behavioral analytics</li>
        <li>Location data</li>
        <li>Device information (model, OS version, identifiers)</li>
        <li>Advertising identifiers</li>
        <li>Crash reports or diagnostics</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>NStates stores a minimal amount of data locally on your device to enable authentication and app functionality:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Authentication tokens:</strong> your nation name, session PIN,
            and autologin token are stored in
            <strong>EncryptedSharedPreferences</strong>, encrypted with AES-256
            and protected by the Android Keystore. These tokens are used to
            authenticate with the NationStates API without requiring you to
            re-enter your password each time.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>User-Agent string:</strong> a configurable identifier sent with
            API requests, stored in Jetpack DataStore. By default it contains no
            personal information.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        <strong>Your password is never stored.</strong> It is sent once over HTTPS
        during login and immediately cleared from memory after authentication.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Network communications</h2>
    <p>
        All network traffic goes exclusively to a single domain:
        <code>https://www.nationstates.net</code>. The app communicates with the
        official NationStates API over HTTPS to:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Authenticate your nation (login and session resume)</li>
        <li>Fetch your nation's profile data (name, flag, statistics, government, economy)</li>
        <li>Retrieve and respond to legislative issues</li>
        <li>Load nation flag and issue banner images</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        No data is sent to any other server. There are no analytics endpoints,
        advertising networks, or third-party services receiving data from the app.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>NStates does not integrate any third-party tracking, analytics, or advertising services. Specifically:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>No advertising SDKs (no AdMob, no ad networks)</li>
        <li>No analytics services (no Firebase Analytics, no Google Analytics)</li>
        <li>No crash reporting services (no Crashlytics, no Sentry)</li>
        <li>No social media SDKs</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The only external service the app communicates with is the official
        <a href="https://www.nationstates.net/pages/api.html" target="_blank" class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80">NationStates API</a>,
        which is governed by its own
        <a href="https://www.nationstates.net/page=privacy" target="_blank" class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data security</h2>
    <p>Your data is protected through:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Encrypted storage:</strong> authentication tokens are encrypted
            at rest using AES-256-GCM, with keys managed by the Android Keystore
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>HTTPS only:</strong> all communication with NationStates uses
            encrypted HTTPS connections
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Password handling:</strong> your password is never written to
            disk and is cleared from memory immediately after login
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>App isolation:</strong> all stored data is in the app's private
            storage, inaccessible to other apps on non-rooted devices
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. App permissions</h2>
    <p>NStates requests only one permission:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Internet access:</strong> required to communicate with the
            NationStates API and load images
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The app does not request access to contacts, camera, microphone, location,
        storage, phone state, or any other sensitive permissions.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Logout and data deletion</h2>
    <p>
        When you log out from the app, all locally stored authentication data
        (nation name, session PIN, autologin token) is immediately and
        permanently deleted from the device.
    </p>
    <p>
        Uninstalling the app removes all associated data, including encrypted
        preferences, DataStore settings, and any cached images.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Backup and synchronization</h2>
    <p>
        NStates does not provide cloud backup or synchronization features. Your
        device's operating system may include the app's data in automatic backups
        (e.g., Google Drive backup), but encrypted authentication tokens would
        not be functional on a different device due to hardware-bound encryption
        keys.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
        NStates does not knowingly collect any data from children. The app does
        not collect personal data from any user. NationStates itself has its own
        age and usage policies.
    </p>

    <h2>11. User rights</h2>
    <p>Since NStates does not collect or store personal data on any server, you always have complete control:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Access:</strong> all stored data is visible through your device
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Deletion:</strong> log out to clear authentication data, or
            uninstall the app to remove everything
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Portability:</strong> no personal data is held on our servers
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        For data held by NationStates itself, refer to the
        <a href="https://www.nationstates.net/page=privacy" target="_blank" class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80">NationStates Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>Any changes to this privacy policy will be communicated through:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>App updates on the Google Play Store</li>
        <li>Publication of the updated version on this page</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>13. Regulatory compliance</h2>
    <p>NStates is designed to comply with:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>CCPA (California Consumer Privacy Act)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Other applicable privacy regulations</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="my-5 rounded-md border-l-4 border-emerald-500/80 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <strong>Remember:</strong> NStates does not collect any personal data. All
        authentication data is stored encrypted on your device and is never sent to
        any server other than the official NationStates API.
    </div>

    <div slot="additional-contact">
        <p>
            For matters related to your NationStates account data, contact
            NationStates directly at
            <a
                href="https://www.nationstates.net/page=help"
                target="_blank" class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80">NationStates Help</a
            >.
        </p>
    </div>
</PrivacyLayout>
